=====================================================================
A. RESPONSIVE UI
=====================================================================
Principle: layout follows the space available, never the device name. Detect with `matchMedia` change events
(one render per breakpoint crossing, not resize spam). Window classes:
  compact  <600px        phones, foldable cover screen
  medium   600-1023px    tablet portrait, unfolded foldable, small windows
  expanded >=1024px      laptops, desktops, tablet landscape
  extra    >=1280px      Markets screen switches to two independent columns
  wide     >=1536px      content stops growing and is centred; extra width becomes margin

Rules that always hold
- Exactly ONE primary navigation at a time: floating dock (compact, medium) OR sidebar (expanded, or a foldable
  spanning two screens). CSS also hides the dock at >=1024px as a safeguard.
- Safe areas: `viewport-fit=cover` in the viewport meta tag; pad header, dock and content with
  `env(safe-area-inset-*)`.
- Fluid spacing: gutter 16 / 24 / 32px (compact / medium / expanded); card padding 12 / 20 / 24px; card radius 20px.
- Type scale: page title 20/24/28px; hero number 30/36/48px with tabular numerals; labels 12px uppercase; body 14px;
  nothing below 12px.
- Never hide a layout bug with `overflow-x:hidden`. Fix the cause (`min-w-0` on flex/grid children, fixed widths).
  No horizontal page scroll from 320px up. Layout must survive browser zoom to 200%.
- Touch targets 44px on touch screens, 32px with a mouse (`pointer: coarse` / `fine`).
- Every column and grid child gets `min-width: 0`. Images and charts scale with their container.

PHONE (<600px): single column, compact cards (about 1.5 screens tall), floating glass dock, tap a card to enlarge it
(already implemented; keep). Header = title + 44px icon buttons + Live chip + avatar; no price strip, no theme button.
TABLET (600-1023px): same dock (wider), 24px gutters, header gains the search field, theme button and a slim live
price strip (horizontally scrollable, no auto-moving marquee). One column; Sentiment | AI side by side; indicators
and trend side by side; watchlist 3-6 card grid.
FOLDABLES: cover screen = Phone. Unfolded flat = Tablet. Spanning two screens (media query
`(horizontal-viewport-segments: 2)`): sidebar in the left screen, content in the right, an empty gutter exactly the
hinge width using `env(viewport-segment-width/left/right)`; nothing crosses the hinge; modals, toasts and enlarged
views open inside ONE screen; the dock is hidden. Browsers without the API fall back to width-based layouts.

LAPTOP RESPONSIVE FACTORS (everything that is added or changes at >=1024px)
1. Navigation swap: the dock disappears and a 256px sticky glass sidebar appears: brand slot, Primary list, a
