=====================================================================
B. LIQUID GLASS LIGHT (moving light on glass)
=====================================================================
Goal: the glass should feel lit and alive, subtly. Three layers, all CSS-driven:
1. Ambient drift: the coloured light behind the app (`.app-root::before`) slowly drifts and breathes
   (32s, ease-in-out, alternate; translate up to about 2.5% and scale 1 to 1.08). Only `transform` animates.
2. Specular sweep: a soft diagonal highlight slides across the hero card and the dock every ~10s (it moves during
   the last 45% of the cycle and rests for the first 55%; the dock is offset by 2.5s so they never flash together).
   Dark: white at 20% peak. Light: white at 65% peak. It sits above the glass fill and below the content.
3. Pointer light (mouse and trackpad only): the card under the pointer gets a soft radial highlight (240px) that
   follows the pointer and fades in 250ms; it is invisible on touch devices. Implemented by the `usePointerLight`
   hook, which writes `--mx` and `--my` to the hovered `.ps-card` (hero excluded, it already has the sweep).
Rules: never animate `backdrop-filter` or blur radius; no infinite animation on every card; nothing flashes faster than
once every 3 seconds (WCAG 2.3.1); `prefers-reduced-motion` = no drift, no sweep, static light;
`prefers-reduced-transparency` / `prefers-contrast: more` = all light overlays removed; text contrast must stay
at or above 4.5:1 while the highlight passes behind it (keep peak opacity at or below the values above).

=====================================================================
C. BOTTOM BAR: LIQUID SHIFT ANIMATION
=====================================================================
Goal: the active-tab highlight is one glass droplet ("lens") that moves between tabs like liquid.
- One lens element (`aria-hidden`) positioned from the active tab's measured left and width (ResizeObserver, so
  rotation, unfolding and font loading re-measure automatically). No per-tab backgrounds.
- Movement: transform + width transition 550ms with an overshoot spring `cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)`.
- Stretch: while it travels, the lens briefly stretches (`scale` 1 to 1.2 wide and 0.93 tall at 35%, back to 1), 550ms.
- Light moves with it: the lens carries its own specular highlight (radial white at the top) and a coloured glow
  underneath (green in dark, warm brown in light), so the "light" shifts with the selection.
- Icon response: the active icon lifts 1px and scales to 1.12 with the same spring; pressing any tab squishes it to 0.94.
- "More": when the More sheet opens the lens slides to More, and slides back to the active tab when it closes.
- First paint: no slide-in from the left (`data-ready` is set one frame after the first measurement).
- Accessibility: keep `aria-current="page"` on the active tab, visible 12px labels, 52px tall targets, focus rings.
  `prefers-reduced-motion` = the lens jumps instantly with no stretch, no spring, no squish.
- Dark and light variants; the dock stays hidden at >=1024px and on spanned foldables.
- No animation library, no layout shift, no timers longer than 560ms.

